-- title:
--   Nilpotent Hasse–Witt matrix kills low-degree coefficients of [p^A]_F
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime, and suppose $\mathcal O$ carries an algebra structure over $\mathbb Z/p$ such that the kernel of $\mathrm{algebraMap}\colon\mathcal O\to\mathbb Z/p$ is the ideal generated by $p$. Let $d\in\mathbb N$ and let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal O$ in the sense of [`MvFormalGroup`](def/MvFormalGroup_BasicV2.html#L15): a family $F_i$, $i\in\mathrm{Fin}\,d$, of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d\oplus\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with zero constant coefficient, with the coefficient of each degree-one monomial $X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}$ and of each $X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}$ equal to $\delta_{ij}$, and satisfying associativity expressed by the two substitutions of $F$ into $F$; assume also `F.IsComm`, i.e. substituting the swap of the two blocks of variables into each $F_i$ returns $F_i$. Write $[n]_F$ for `F.nthSeries n`, the family in $d$ variables defined by $[0]_F=0$ and $[n+1]_F=F\bigl([n]_F(X),X\bigr)$. Assume the matrix in $M_d(\mathbb Z/p)$ whose $(i,j)$ entry is the image of the coefficient of $X_j^{\,p}$ in $[p]_{F,i}$ is nilpotent. Then there is an integer $A\ge 1$ such that for every $i$ and every exponent vector $n\colon\mathrm{Fin}\,d\to_{0}\mathbb N$ of total degree $<p^{A+1}$, the coefficient of $X^n$ in $[p^A]_{F,i}$ lies in the ideal generated by $p$ in $\mathcal O$.
--
--   This is the integral form of the statement that, when the Hasse–Witt matrix of the reduction of $F$ is nilpotent, the multiplication-by-$p^A$ series of $F$ is congruent to $0$ modulo $p$ in all monomials of total degree below $p^{A+1}$. It feeds the slope estimate [`MvFormalGroup.exists_coeff_mem_span_pow_sub_log_of_isNilpotent_hasseWitt`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_coeff_mem_span_pow_sub_log_of_isNilpotent_hasseWitt).
